CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F398A1785853117
OL,3,CMayors react to Andy Burnham's plans
OL,4,Cto give them share of income tax
OL,6,FThe North East Mayor, Labour's Kim
OL,7,FMcGuinness, has warmly welcomed the
OL,8,Fplans, saying "this is what we've been
OL,9,Ffighting for".
OL,11,FShe said: "For decades, whenever the
OL,12,FNorth wanted something, it had to go
OL,13,Fto London each time, cap in hand to
OL,14,Fbeg a civil servant or a Government
OL,15,Fminister to back us.
OL,17,F"The days of asking Whitehall's
OL,18,Fpermission are over. We can now just
OL,19,Fget on with the job and improve the
OL,20,Flives of people here in the North
OL,21,FEast, now and for generations to come."
OL,1,W~k4~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}        G2/6
OL,2,W/*%+, "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNE Eng NewsCThis Day FReg TV
FL,399,390,120,260,000,100
PN,39803
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F398A1785853117
OL,3,CMayors react to Andy Burnham's plans
OL,4,Cto give them share of income tax
OL,6,FBut Lord Houchen, the Conservative
OL,7,FTees Valley Mayor, has said he would
OL,8,Frather be able to give this money back
OL,9,Fto people as tax rebates, or ideally
OL,10,Flower the rate of income tax in his
OL,11,Fregion.
OL,13,FHe said: "Young people are out of work
OL,14,Fin record levels, businesses are
OL,15,Fclosing, economies are struggling, and
OL,16,Fthe easiest way is to just give people
OL,17,Fa little bit of relief by being able
OL,18,Fto keep that money, put it in their
OL,19,Fpocket, allow businesses a bit of
OL,20,Fbreathing space.
OL,1,W~k4~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}        G3/6
OL,2,W/*%+, "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNE Eng NewsCThis Day FReg TV
FL,399,390,120,260,000,100
PN,39804
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F398A1785853117
OL,3,CMayors react to Andy Burnham's plans
OL,4,Cto give them share of income tax
OL,6,F"It just seems a much simpler way than
OL,7,Fhaving to take it off people, to give
OL,8,Fit back to them."
OL,10,FMeanwhile, David Skaith, Mayor of York
OL,11,Fand North Yorkshire, backed the
OL,12,Fproposals, describing them as the
OL,13,F"biggest shift of powers,
OL,14,Fresponsibilities and resources from
OL,15,FWestminster to local leaders" ever.
OL,17,FHe said: "The voices of people,
OL,18,Fcommunities, and businesses across our
OL,19,Fcounty will be heard more clearly than
OL,20,Fever before.
OL,1,W~k4~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}        G4/6
OL,2,W/*%+, "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNE Eng NewsCThis Day FReg TV
FL,399,390,120,260,000,100
PN,39805
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F398A1785853117
OL,3,CMayors react to Andy Burnham's plans
OL,4,Cto give them share of income tax
OL,6,F"This shift in power will help us to
OL,7,Fmake sure we can tackle the issues
OL,8,Fthat hold us back the most."
OL,10,FDetails of the reforms are expected to
OL,11,Fbe announced in a white paper,
OL,12,Fpublished when Chancellor John Healey
OL,13,Fpresents his first budget. It has been
OL,14,Frevealed today (31 July) that this
OL,15,Fwill be delivered on Wednesday 28
OL,16,FOctober.
OL,18,FThe rate of income tax which
OL,19,Fbillpayers face will not change as a
OL,20,Fdirect result of the reforms,
OL,21,Faccording to the Government.
OL,1,W~k4~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}        G5/6
OL,2,W/*%+, "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,,,,,,
